    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0734" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5742: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-16T14:00:00-05:00">February 16, 1933—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your 141, February 13, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="88" xml:id="d683-f1"/> and previous.
                    The Department is disposed to adopt the suggestion contained in your 139,
                    February 13, noon; on the condition, however, that preferential lien of loan
                    under reference must not adversely affect payment of any obligation of the
                    Chinese Government held by this Government and/or by American citizens. The
                    American Government might, however, <pb facs="0735" n="633" xml:id="pg633"/>
                    feel obliged sooner or later to lodge a reservation or protest with regard to
                    any American rights that may be found to have been adversely affected.</p>
                <p>You may at your discretion explain our position, as above, to your French
                    colleague.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
